{
  "id": "double-pendulum-phy",
  "name": "Double Pendulum",
  "description": "A chaotic double pendulum system demonstrating sensitive dependence on initial conditions. Two pendulums are connected end-to-end, with the first attached to a fixed pivot point. The system exhibits complex, unpredictable motion characteristic of deterministic chaos. Reference: http://www.myphysicslab.com/dbl_pendulum.html Source reconciliation: explicit shorthand is translated to the existing declared quantities using the pinned native equations; source initial values and 0.0078125-second integration grid are retained. Euler energy drift and chaotic sensitivity limit long-horizon physical accuracy.",
